Subject: Cantor Schema Direction Input Audit

@ [audit_uuid] a79bb5d5-f611-4e8f-b446-ab193d2f4002
@ [source_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-05_cantor_schema_direction_profile\Source_Document_Manifest.sop

& [ObservedLibrary] is exact schemars 1.2.2
  + SchemaSettings defaults to the Deserialize contract
  + for_serialize selects the Serialize contract
  + SchemaUid includes contract as well as type identity
  + recursive definition caching is therefore contract-sensitive

& [ObservedTransport] is directional
  + PrepareRequest, PreparedRunRequest as run input, and VerifyRequest are decoded from caller bytes
  + ProcedureToolResponse and its base and preparation variants are encoded to response bytes
  + PreparedRunRequest crosses the boundary because it is emitted inside preparation response data and later decoded as run input

& [Conflict] is one unqualified shared-definition universe
  + a stable type name alone cannot identify both direction-specific contracts
  + byte equality across contracts is possible but cannot be assumed
  + one reused local reference may describe emitted shape when accepted shape was required, or the reverse

& [AuditDisposition] is separate_contract_universes_candidate
  + candidate remains non-authorizing until canonical profile, requirements, review, and lock are formed

